Dispatch_ready can be achieved via finalize_candidate_direct or finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation or finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation. Those produce dispatch_ready ?candidate. Also there are actions mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready which set dispatch_ready for origin/destination availability. But for shift_candidate_alpha we need dispatch_ready.

We can also get dispatch_ready via finalize_candidate_direct (requires candidate_clearance_established, not route_sequence_context_set, not candidate_finalized). Or finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_validated). Or finalize_candidate_after_compliance_validation (requires compliance_validation_complete).

